{"name":"Sound of Silence","hex":"#333b33","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sound","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Healthy.","Complete, solid, or secure."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Soundly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sound"},{"term":"silence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The absence of any sound.","The act of refraining from speaking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (someone or something) silent.","To repress the expression of something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sound of Silence (Dami Im song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sound of Silence\" is a song performed by the Australian recording artist Dami Im. Written by Anthony Egizii and David Musumeci of DNA Songs, it is best known as Australia's entry at the Eurovision Song Contest 2016 which was held in Stockholm, Sweden, where it finished 2nd, receiving a total of 511 points. The song also won the Marcel Bezençon Award in the composer category. The song was leaked on 10 March 2016, one day before its initial release date. It is Dami Im's fourth Australian top 20 hit and worldwide, it reached the top 40 in more than six countries after the Eurovision Song Contest 2016 Final."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/47/Dami-im-sound-of-silence-2016-300x300.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound_of_Silence_(Dami_Im_song)"},{"title":"Sound of Silence (2017 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sound of Silence is a 2017 Indian film in Hindi, Pahari and Tibetan. The film is directed by Malayalam film director Bijukumar Damodaran, commonly known as Dr. Biju. The film premiered at the 2017 Montreal World Film Festival. The film won an award for Best Director at the 2017 Kolkata International Film Festival in the Indian Film Competition category."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/Sound_of_Silence_Tibetan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound_of_Silence_(2017_film)"},{"title":"The Sound of Silence","blocks":[{"text":"\"The Sound of Silence\" is a song by the American folk rock duo Simon & Garfunkel, written by Paul Simon. The duo's studio audition of the song led to a record deal with Columbia Records, and the original acoustic version was recorded in March 1964 at Columbia's 7th Avenue Recording Studios in New York City for their debut album, Wednesday Morning, 3 A.M., released that October to disappointing sales. An overdubbed electric remix was released the following year and went to number one on the Billboard singles chart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/The_Sounds_of_Silence_by_Simon_and_Garfunkel_US_vinyl.png/330px-The_Sounds_of_Silence_by_Simon_and_Garfunkel_US_vinyl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sound_of_Silence"},{"title":"Sound","blocks":[{"text":"Sound is a phenomenon in which pressure disturbances propagate through an elastic material medium. In the context of physics, it is characterised as a mechanical wave of pressure or related quantities, whereas in physiological-psychological contexts it implies a hearing process. Though sensitivity to sound varies among all organisms, the human ear is sensitive to audio frequencies ranging from 20 Hz to 20 kHz. More broadly, acoustic waves encompass mechanical longitudinal waves in general.\nExamples of the significance and application of sound include music, medical imaging techniques, oral language and parts of science."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Thoth08BigasDrumEvansChalmette.jpg/330px-Thoth08BigasDrumEvansChalmette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sound"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg/500px-Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg/500px-Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paul Simon, the song's composer, c. 1966","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaul_Simon_in_1966.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Cocoa_Beach_at_Lori_Wilson_Park_-_Flickr_-_Rusty_Clark_%28112%29.jpg/500px-Cocoa_Beach_at_Lori_Wilson_Park_-_Flickr_-_Rusty_Clark_%28112%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Cocoa_Beach_at_Lori_Wilson_Park_-_Flickr_-_Rusty_Clark_%28112%29.jpg/1280px-Cocoa_Beach_at_Lori_Wilson_Park_-_Flickr_-_Rusty_Clark_%28112%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Cocoa_Beach_at_Lori_Wilson_Park_-_Flickr_-_Rusty_Clark_%28112%29.jpg/500px-Cocoa_Beach_at_Lori_Wilson_Park_-_Flickr_-_Rusty_Clark_%28112%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The song's heavy airplay in Cocoa Beach, Florida, alerted Columbia to release the single.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACocoa_Beach_at_Lori_Wilson_Park_-_Flickr_-_Rusty_Clark_(112).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/21/Disturbed_-_The_Sound_of_Silence.jpg/250px-Disturbed_-_The_Sound_of_Silence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/21/Disturbed_-_The_Sound_of_Silence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi